<p>The post <a href="https://gdpr.eu/gdpr-vs-lgpd/">What is the LGPD? Brazil’s version of the GDPR</a> appeared first on <a href="https://gdpr.eu">GDPR.eu</a>.</p>

## Summary
This article explains Brazil's General Data Protection Law (LGPD), which was passed in 2018 and came into effect in February 2020. It compares the LGPD to the European GDPR, highlighting key similarities and differences in data protection regulations.

## Key Points
- The LGPD is Brazil's equivalent to the GDPR, focusing on data protection and privacy rights.
- It was enacted in 2018 and became effective in February 2020, impacting data handling practices.
- The article provides a comparative analysis between LGPD and GDPR to clarify regulatory differences.
- Data protection laws like LGPD and GDPR are essential for ensuring compliance and safeguarding personal data.


